nterval is 10s (maxAge = 30s); request GET /fragments/instance?instance=one; today app_test.go:119 (TestRefreshRetainsLastSuccessfulSnapshotOnFailure) only tests freshness becoming stale when a collector explicitly returns an error; no test exercises the elapsed time decay where a silent or delayed worker causes freshness to decay from fresh to stale. Acceptance: a Builder adds regression tests in app_test.go and server_test.go verifying that an instance whose last success is older than 3 * refreshInterval is classified as Freshness: \\\"stale\\\" despite Err == nil, and that GET /fragments/instance renders the stale badge. Observed: view.go:155 checks !now.Before(state.LastSuccess.Add(maxAge)), but grep shows this elapsed time decay branch is never tested in any *_test.go file. Required: regression tests in app_test.go and server_test.go covering elapsed-time freshness decay to stale when refresh attempts stall or cease. Proposed test-work: add tests in app_test.go and server_test.go verifying that instances decay to stale freshness when elapsed time exceeds three refresh intervals without a new successful snapshot.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": null,\n  \"promoted_at\": null,\n  \"promotions\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:21.987Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-04T19:39:26.217Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": false,\n    \"takeable\": false\n  }\n}\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788550766257},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.encrypted\",\"data\":\"\",\"format\":\"google-gemini-v1\",\"id\":\"call_381683\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_381683","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"powder create --id canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation --title 'CLI envelope schema version mismatch and envelope malformed JSON rejection lack regression cover' --repo 