ragments/instance`, Collection warnings, and Trigger matrix state badges.\n- **Log Presentation:** `server.go`, `templates/log.html`, and `server_test.go` — evaluated `GET /logs` fragment states across retained, evicted, unknown, and error conditions.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Findings Filed\n\nFiled exactly five SPEC-LESS draft Powder jobs (no `--spec` passed; all jobs remain unleased and non-takeable):\n\n1. **`canopy-tester-inventory-validation-bounds`**\n   - **Surface:** `inventory.go:59` (`validateListen`), `inventory.go:68-75` (interval bounds), `inventory.go:76` (empty instances array), via `LoadInventory(path)`.\n   - **Untested Behavior:** `LoadInventory` validates operational configuration parameters and must reject invalid inputs: listen addresses missing a port (e.g. `127.0.0.1`), non-numeric ports, ports outside `1..65535` (`0` or `70000`), whitespace/control characters, negative `fleet_interval_seconds` / `selected_interval_seconds`, and empty instances arrays (`\"instances\": []`).\n   - **Required Test:** Table-driven regression tests in `inventory_test.go` asserting rejection and specific error messages for invalid listen syntax, port range violations, negative intervals, and empty instances arrays.\n\n2. **`canopy-tester-freshness-elapsed-decay`**\n   - **Surface:** `view.go:148` (`classifyFreshness`), `view.go:194` (`instanceView`), `view.go:171` (`pageView`), routes `GET /` and `GET /fragments/instance`.\n   - **Untested Behavior:** When an instance has a valid prior snapshot (`state.Snapshot != nil`) and no new error (`state.Err == nil`), but background collection has ceased or delayed beyond the threshold (`now >= LastSuccess + maxAge`, where `maxAge = 3 * refreshInterval`), Canopy must classify its freshness as `\"stale\"` and render `<span class=\"status-badge stale\">` and `<span class=\"state-dot stale\">` instead of `\"fresh\"`.\n   - **Required Test:** Regression tests in `app_test.go` and `server_test.go` proving that an instance without recent success decays to stale freshness after three refresh intervals expire without an error being reported.\n\n3. **`canopy-tester-envelope-schema-validation`**\n   - **Surface:** `collector.go:297` (`cliCollector.runJSON`), `collector.go:343` (`decodeCLIEnvelope`), `collector.go:138` (`cliCollector.Collect`).\n   - **Untested Behavior:** Canopy strictly requires the `forest.cli.v2` wire protocol. Command output with an incompatible schema (e.g. `\"forest.cli.v1\"`), missing top-level envelope fields (`schema`, `command`, `args`, `exit`), or trailing JSON must be rejected with a `*CLIError` stating the schema mismatch or envelope error, and terminate collection.\n   - **Required Test:** Unit tests in `collector_test.go` verifying that `Collect` returns a `*CLIError` when envelope schema does not match `\"forest.cli.v2\"`, required envelope fields are missing, or trailing JSON exists.\n\n4. **`canopy-tester-trigger-matrix-warnings`**\n   - **Surface:** `view.go:245-260` (`instanceView`), `view.go:332-348` (`triggerViews`), `templates/instance.html:10-16` (Collection warnings), `templates/instance.html:66-77` (Trigger matrix), route `GET /fragments/instance`.\n   - **Untested Behavior:** When an instance snapshot contains Kernel lock errors (`Kernel.LockError`), trigger state errors, or trigger poll/run/audit errors: (1) Canopy must render the \"Collection warnings\" section with `<span class=\"signal error\">attention</span>` listing each warning; (2) in the \"Trigger matrix\" table, each trigger row must render poll status badges (`error`, `stale`, `unknown`), run status badges, and consecutive error counts.\n   - **Required Test:** HTTP handler regression tests in `server_test.go` asserting that `GET /fragments/instance` renders the Collection warnings section for lock/trigger errors and renders expected signal badges in the Trigger matrix.\n\n5. **`canopy-tester-log-general-error-fragment`**\n   - **Surface:** `server.go:121` (`handleLogs`), `templates/log.html:18` (error state card), route `GET /logs`.\n   - **Untested Behavior:** When `GET /logs?instance=<id>&run=<id>` is requested and `Collector.Logs` returns a non-exit-4 failure (e.g. exit 1, I/O error, or timeout), Canopy must return HTTP 200 with the log drawer fragment rendering `State = \"error\"`, badge `<span class=\"signal error\">error</span>`, headline `<p>Canopy could not read this Run log.</p>`, and the error message in `<p class=\"muted\">`, without failing the HTTP response.\n   - **Required Test:** An HTTP regression test in `server_test.go` verifying that non-exit-4 collector errors return HTTP 200 and render the error state drawer fragment.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Findings Skipped as Duplicates\n\n- **Zero-instance empty inventory routes:** Skipped as duplicate of open job `canopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering`.\n- **Initial collection failure freshness & attempted state:** Skipped as duplicate of open job `canopy-tester-initial-collection-failure`.\n- **Route query parameter traversal and character rejection:** Skipped as duplicate of open job `canopy-tester-route-param-validation`.\n- **Retained Run log secret redaction:** Skipped as duplicate of open job `if-critic-log-sanitize-untested` (and previously abandoned job `canopy-tester-log-secret-redaction`).\n- **Audit divergence stale trust override:** Skipped as duplicate of completed job `canopy-tester-audit-divergence-stale`.\n- **Collector follow polling loop:** Skipped as duplicate of open/superseded job `if-critic-dead-collector-surface`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Findings Discarded for Lack of Evidence\n\n- **Older Forest omitted-name fallback (`collector.go:212`):** `declaration.Name == \"\"` fallback is an internal backward-compatibility branch rather than a user-observable failure boundary.\n- **Recent runs reverse ordering (`view.go:228`):** Rendering newest-first is observable, but lower risk and secondary to operational warning and trigger matrix coverage.\n- **Ledger agent aggregate table rendering (`templates/instance.html:92`):** Discarded in favor of the higher-impact Collection warnings and Trigger matrix findings within the 5-job filing cap.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Worktree State\n\nNo files were edited, no branches were created, and no commits or pushes were made. Working tree is clean."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","usage":{"input":4918,"output":2734,"cacheRead":83601,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":774,"totalTokens":91253,"cost":{"input":0.004672099999999999,"output":0.010936,"cacheRead":0.01337616,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.028984259999999998}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1788550792146,"responseId":"gen-1788550792-XTEfso4CZjBwroby7L2h","rawStopReason":"stop"}],"willRetry":false}
